 Or better yet "My kingdom for a bell of opening!"

 Yes, I've discovered another cruelty to the game. I decided "Right!
Time to give the Tourist class a try. I'm ready." Errr... yeah.
Well, after losing 9 1/2 million tourists to any and all forms of death,
I finally got one going. An early discovery of a shield of reflection and 
this one was off to the races. And having the luck of a co-aligned alter
in the gnomish mine town turn into a gift of mjollnir after sacrificing
for awhile made things even better. The quest came and my tourist
plowed through it, even killing shop keepers just for extra stuff
(boy, the quest is filled with supplies isn't it?). A few turns
and the nemesis was dead. There's the PYEC and...
  That is correct, I'm playing on a system with version 3.1.0! What
this means, I discovered much too late, is that due to a glitch,
the tourist' nemesis doesn't carry a bell of opening. So I'm doomed.

  I went ahead on down and plundered the castle, grabbed the wand of 
wishing and wished for "Bell of Opening" and received "a bell". Well,
I then wished for "a silver bell" and received "a bell". Oh dear...

  So what should I do now? Should I: be stubborn and try to keep the
game going for months, maybe hoping to genocide all the monsters 
through random process? or be nasty, grab a couple of cursed scrolls
of genocide and create a most interesting bones file of black
dragons and master liches? or do like a true tourist would and
say "to hell with it" and just exit the dungeon?

  In the meantime, would anyone like to fed.ex. a bell of opening 
down to level 55 of gehennom?


